# Copy to .env (git-ignored) or export these. NOTHING here is committed.
#
# WHICH ENVIRONMENT ------------------------------------------------------------
# The suite reads whatever this names. Everything else follows from it.
GS_APP=https://app.staging.shopview.com
# The API host is derived from GS_APP (app.x -> api.x). Set it only if that is wrong.
# GS_API=api.staging.shopview.com

# SIGNING IN -------------------------------------------------------------------
# STAGING AND QA BRANCHES — ONE VALUE. Sign in to the environment in any browser,
# DevTools > Application > Cookies, and copy the value of `sv_sso_session` here.
# Every run then signs itself in with no window and no person (it calls the
# quick-login endpoint behind that cookie). Never paste it into chat or commit it.
# GS_SSO=...
#
# The permission checks' second person off production is quick-login's `tech` key
# (a Technician: work orders + customers/assets, no parts/part sales/vendors).
# GS_LIMITED_KEY=tech
#
# EASIEST ON STAGING: don't put anything below. Run `npm run login`, sign in with
# Google in the browser it opens, and the whole session (cookies AND localStorage)
# is saved to .auth/<host>.json, which is git-ignored and reused by every run.
# Redo it when the saved session expires; the suite says so in those words.
# GS_AUTH_STATE=/path/to/session.json   # only to keep it somewhere else
#
# PRODUCTION uses a username and password.
# GS_USER=someone@shopview.com
# GS_PASS=...
#
# STAGING uses Google sign-in, so there is no password to script. Take a live
# session's cookies from a signed-in browser (DevTools > Application > Cookies)
# and put them here. They expire — a Google sign-in screen means take a fresh set.
# GS_SSO=...          # sv_sso_session
# GS_PHPSESSID=...    # PHPSESSID — staging needs this one too, unlike a QA branch
# GS_CF=...           # cf_clearance, only if Cloudflare is in front
#
# Cookies authenticate the API, but the APP keeps its session in localStorage and staging signs in
# through Google — so cookies alone leave the browser on the login screen. From the same signed-in
# browser: DevTools > Application > Local Storage > app.staging.shopview.com, and copy:
# GS_STAGING_USER={"data":{...}}   # the whole value of the `user` key, as it appears
# GS_STAGING_TOKEN=...             # the `token` key, if there is one

# Instead of the above you may point at a file holding SV_USER=/SV_PASS= or
# SV_SSO_SESSION=/PHPSESSID=/CF_CLEARANCE=, kept outside the repository:
# GS_ENVF=/path/to/credentials.env
# GS_STAGING_ENVF=/path/to/staging-cookies.env

# THE PERMISSION CHECKS --------------------------------------------------------
# They compare a full-access person with a lower-permission one. Without this
# second account those checks stand down and say so; everything else still runs.
# GS_LIMITED_ENVF=/path/to/lower-permission-credentials.env

# THE PREFLIGHT ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Before the first test, the run checks that the records the checks look for are on the
# environment, and STOPS if they are not. `npm run preflight` asks the same question on
# its own. It creates nothing.
# GS_PREFLIGHT=warn   # report what is missing, run anyway, those checks stand down
# GS_PREFLIGHT=off    # skip the check entirely

# SEEDING ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# `npm test` seeds the environment before the first test, every run. Needs Python 3.8+.
# GS_SEED=check        # measure only, create nothing
# GS_SEED=skip         # do not seed (re-running one spec on data you just seeded)
# GS_SEED_CACHE=...    # where record ids are kept between runs (default ~/.cache/shopview-e2e)
# GS_PYTHON=python3    # a specific Python
#
# The seeder and the tests sign into the shop the data lives in — parts search is
# scoped by shop. Defaults: staging "Staging Heavy Duty", production "Trucks Hill 2".
# GS_WORKPLACE=Staging Heavy Duty

# OPTIONAL ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# GS_SEED_ALLOW_PROD=1   # the seeder refuses production unless this is set
# CHROME_BIN=/path/to/chrome   # only if Playwright's own browser cannot be used
# GS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:8080   # only if this machine needs a proxy to reach the app
